WEBVTT

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:01.740
Thank you.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:59.980
A band of ruthless criminals, the mysterious and mad...

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:05.470
Gargoyle, backed by millions from an unknown power, attempts to wreck production for national

00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:11.190
defense. The police, baffled, seek the aid of Richard Wentworth, the famous amateur criminologist.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:17.060
Sometimes masquerading as the spider, thus concealing his identity from both criminals

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:22.760
and the police, went his wits and strength against the Gargoyle in preventing sabotage,

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:28.930
subversive activities, and other crimes. Blinky traps a gangster into leading him to his boss,

00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:29.830
where he can

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.120
Front the gargoyle face to mask for a showdown.

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:00.650
Come on.

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:15.420
badly hurt? No, only fainted. In another minute, we would have been done for. Did you miss the trail?

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:19.220
No, we followed at the cave opening, but our radio broke down. We had to race back and get Commissioner Kirk

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:22.740
and his men. That's too bad. If our plans had worked out, we would have caught the gargoyle.

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:29.920
That's all right, Nita. It's all over. This is the only one we could catch, Commissioner. The others got away.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:34.960
The others don't count. This is the one we're after. You've caught the gargoyle, and you'll all be promoted.

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:37.260
Not so fast, Kirk. You're taking too much for granted.

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:41.580
Nonsense. He fits every description. He must be the gargoyle.

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:48.120
Just as I thought. The gargoyle is far away. This man has a decoy to cover his escape.

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:52.320
He'll pay for it. I'll make him talk if I have to skin him alive.

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:55.720
Don't wait your time, Kirk. Send him in well-guarded. The gargoyle may be waiting to kill him.

00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:57.220
I'll take him along, boys.

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:03.280
Commissioner, I'm going to use that prisoner of yours tonight.

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:04.160
Oh, I say.

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:05.580
You've done enough for one night.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:06.340
Take it easy, Dick.

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:07.880
Yes, Dick, you need a rest.

00:04:08.170 --> 00:04:09.110
Does the gargoyle rest?

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:10.890
I'm going to question this man, Cahill,

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:12.090
and the presence of the whole committee.

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:14.310
You still think the guilty man is among them?

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:14.910
I am certain.

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:16.510
Nita, get your list.

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:17.550
Phone every member of the committee

00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:18.710
and tell them to be at the club in an hour.

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:20.170
Tell them what we're going to do, too.

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:21.930
It's not Cahill.

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:23.250
They're going to question it.

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:25.670
Give me that glove you made with the fingerprints on it.

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:26.480
But I...

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:27.460
Get me that glove!

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:33.140
Don't you believe you want to take it over?

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:34.660
Cahill's a good man.

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:36.660
Since when do you question my ass?

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:37.720
Give me that glove.

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:39.120
All right.

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:40.290
There it is.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:41.340
And it's perfect.

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:44.050
But somehow I hope your plan fails.

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:49.160
Gentlemen, take your places.

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:11.740
Well, Cartwright, it's a good thing you showed up.

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:13.860
We were beginning to think weird things about you.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.900
I'm sorry I was late. I had a blowout.

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:17.420
Fine time you pick for it.

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:19.120
Gentlemen, let us proceed.

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:23.800
Because of the importance of this case, we'll make a deal.

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:26.920
We'll turn you loose and afford your protection,

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:29.960
provided you tell us everything you know about the...

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:36.260
this gargoyle. That's just dandy. Then the gargoyle finished me. Not a chance. I love

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:44.030
living, so I'm keeping my trap shut. All right so far. Cahill ain't chirping. So, it's your

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:48.780
fear of the gargoyle's vengeance that keeps you from talking. Yeah, if you must know,

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:52.880
yeah. All right, we'll remove that fear. Bring him in.

00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:04.400
Now will you talk, or will you foolishly share his fate?

00:06:04.810 --> 00:06:06.810
I'll talk. I'll tell you everything I know.

00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:08.250
I'll turn safe evidence.

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:09.680
I ain't gonna take the boat.

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:13.300
You won't get her.

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:15.250
Now you answer my questions.

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:16.870
Talk fast and give me the truth.

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:18.820
Where is this man's headquarters?

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:20.760
You'll never suspect it in the world.

00:06:21.130 --> 00:06:21.950
It's hard to find.

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:24.050
I'll have to take you there so we can get in.

00:06:24.620 --> 00:06:25.380
You go to...

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:26.440
Whatever.

00:06:26.980 --> 00:06:27.100
Whatever.

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:28.240
Whatever.

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:28.920
Whatever.

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:28.960
Whatever.

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:38.170
This man is dead.

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:39.310
Get him!

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:48.610
With his legongle oil.

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:49.490
Use your heads.

00:06:49.910 --> 00:06:52.050
Wentworth framed this to make this man talk.

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:53.390
But he was trying to get away.

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:55.740
I was merely trying to catch the man who pulled the main switch.

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:57.020
Don't touch that gun.

00:06:58.080 --> 00:06:59.980
Cahill was killed with that gun by some...

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:05.110
person in this room his fingerprints must be on it and i'm sending for a fingerprint expert

00:07:05.260 --> 00:07:16.900
meanwhile none of you may leave here or guard that door it's the last of them commissioner and

00:07:16.920 --> 00:07:20.860
none of the fingerprints match the ones on the gun there's a mistake here somewhere the man that

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:25.410
fired that gun must be in this room you've overlooked something commissioner all the

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:29.850
fingerprints have not been taken. Both you and Wentworth have failed to make yours.

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:32.440
What are you talking about, man?

00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:33.620
They were in the room.

00:07:33.780 --> 00:07:35.780
He's right, and I apologize.

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:39.000
And I assure you that Mr. Wentworth agrees with me.

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:39.480
Certainly.

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:41.010
Take mine.

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:49.200
You're in the clear, Commissioner.

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:50.300
Different class entirely.

00:07:51.350 --> 00:07:54.150
Well, Wentworth, he doesn't look too good for me.

00:08:02.810 --> 00:08:05.900
Well, sorry, sir. This is a perfect match.

00:08:06.180 --> 00:08:07.360
Why? You!

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:10.200
Gentlemen, please. This is an outrage.

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:13.070
I'm sure that Mr. Wentworth will explain.

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:16.240
There's nothing to explain. Facts seem to speak for themselves.

00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:18.560
Wentworth of all things I ever heard.

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:22.310
Well, Commissioner, it's obvious that Wentworth is the gargoyle.

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:23.600
What do you intend to do?

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:26.540
I refuse to believe that Mr. Wentworth is guilty.

00:08:27.070 --> 00:08:29.970
He is the one man that has risked his life many times to bring...

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:37.040
the gargoyle to justice that's right the one we least suspect is the guilty man in many cases

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:42.340
i'm sure mr wentworth won't mind being held in technical custody until the matter couldn't be

00:08:42.340 --> 00:08:52.020
cleaned up what do you intend to do wentworth i'm on the spot i know you are innocent but it's best

00:08:52.020 --> 00:08:57.100
that i place you under technical arrest you don't object do you certainly not if you can catch me

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:08.370
He's Wentworth.

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:09.450
I haven't the least idea.

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:10.430
Don't stall.

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:11.960
You've seen the headlines.

00:09:12.470 --> 00:09:15.310
Wentworth has made me the laughing stock of the entire city.

00:09:15.550 --> 00:09:16.850
I'm searching this place.

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:17.890
Help yourself, Commissioner.

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:18.570
Upstairs.

00:09:30.890 --> 00:09:33.670
Wait! Certainly, that's nothing new. He's an investigator.

00:09:41.190 --> 00:09:41.850
What do you make of this?

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:44.640
Commissioner Kirk record, number 12.

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:47.170
Huh, well, I'll soon find out.

00:09:53.950 --> 00:09:56.050
Commissioner, sorry to make you wait. What's on your mind?

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:59.980
Sorry, Commissioner, I can't talk to you now. I'm busy with an important experience.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:09.360
permit. I'll get in touch with you later. Sorry, old man. Goodbye. Come here, you. I see everything

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:15.020
now. This explains his many stereotype phone conversations. Explains how a man can be in

00:10:15.020 --> 00:10:19.590
two places at once. But I can explain it. Wentworth's the man to explain. Instead, he

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:25.750
runs away. Shame on you, Kirk. And you, a commissioner of police. That's all, my boys.

00:10:25.870 --> 00:10:29.970
I'll explain. See here, Wentworth. You've made a monkey out of me. Oh, that's...

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:34.190
all right but last night has to be cleared up the fingerprints on that gun

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:40.950
science doesn't laugh sometimes scientists do commissioner here are my

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:44.210
fingerprints placed there by the gargoyle I picked it up where he threw it

00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:48.680
away after the murder well this will clear up everything I'll explain it to

00:10:48.680 --> 00:10:52.380
the newspapers you'll explain nothing to the newspapers I'm going to remain a

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:56.000
fugitive from justice for a while yet for what reason to give the gargoyle

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:59.300
confidence his gang is small now and he'll try to strike while the tide is

00:10:59.300 --> 00:10:59.880
running his way

00:11:00.350 --> 00:11:01.110
I hope to stop it.

00:11:01.310 --> 00:11:04.950
And in the meantime, the papers continue to call me a nitwit.

00:11:05.620 --> 00:11:06.740
You can take it, Commissioner.

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:09.620
The papers will be the first to praise you when you bring in the gargoyle.

00:11:12.870 --> 00:11:13.270
Hello.

00:11:13.720 --> 00:11:16.060
Uncle was called to a mysterious meeting of the committee

00:11:16.060 --> 00:11:18.810
at West Falls Experimental Plant No. 3.

00:11:19.050 --> 00:11:20.170
Well, that's nothing to worry about.

00:11:20.370 --> 00:11:21.510
They're financing his new experiment.

00:11:21.770 --> 00:11:24.470
But he had no sooner left than a mysterious voice phone

00:11:24.470 --> 00:11:27.130
and warned me that they had all gone into a trap

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:29.520
and the gargoyle intended to kill them all.

00:11:29.770 --> 00:11:29.970
All right.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.780
All right. Thanks, Nita. I'll act at once.

00:11:32.010 --> 00:11:33.730
Now, you stay close to the house. I'll send Jackson over.

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:37.020
Jackson, get to Nita. Don't bother, but keep a close watch on the house.

00:11:37.180 --> 00:11:38.020
Get the car ready, Ramsey.

00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:39.200
And what now?

00:11:39.530 --> 00:11:41.930
I just received a tip that the gargoyle's going to act sooner than I expected.

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:42.810
I can't explain now.

00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:48.040
That's the way he always acts.

00:11:48.830 --> 00:11:50.450
Sorry, Commissioner. I can't talk to you now.

00:11:50.700 --> 00:11:52.140
I'm busy with an important experiment.

00:11:52.180 --> 00:11:53.200
I'll get in touch with you later.

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:54.040
Sorry, old man.

00:12:02.110 --> 00:12:03.870
Gentlemen, I tell you I didn't call you.

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:06.250
My telegram is signed by Commissioner Kirk.

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:08.050
But your name is on my telegram.

00:12:08.190 --> 00:12:09.310
I have it here to prove it.

00:12:09.350 --> 00:12:10.190
That doesn't prove anything.

00:12:10.350 --> 00:12:11.550
My wire was signed by you.

00:12:11.670 --> 00:12:13.010
It's a conspiracy of some sort.

00:12:13.070 --> 00:12:14.550
My telegram was signed by Cartwright.

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:15.150
Cartwright?

00:12:16.490 --> 00:12:17.770
He's the only one that isn't here.

00:12:18.610 --> 00:12:18.970
Cartwright.

00:12:19.860 --> 00:12:21.020
Cartwright's the gargoyle.

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:23.070
He enticed us here for some reason or other.

00:12:23.310 --> 00:12:24.370
This is no time to argue.

00:12:24.490 --> 00:12:25.190
Let's get out of here.

00:12:25.270 --> 00:12:25.830
Come on, let's go.

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:29.480
Why, gentlemen, what's wrong?

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:31.530
Cartwright, don't try anything.

00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:32.690
We're four to one.

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:34.970
We fell for your telegram, but that doesn't mean we won't fight.

00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:37.650
Well, Stan, I was summoned here, too.

00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:39.440
The wire said it was urgent.

00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:40.440
Who was it signed by?

00:12:40.600 --> 00:12:42.140
Like by Wentworth, of course.

00:12:43.660 --> 00:12:45.560
No one ever betrayed the gargoyle before.

00:12:46.020 --> 00:12:47.180
I'm sure it's a trap.

00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:49.060
Won't be the first one, Moyer.

00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:51.610
Well, you have me frightened, too.

00:12:51.730 --> 00:12:54.370
We shouldn't remain here as we are, surrounded by Westfall's explosives.

00:12:54.550 --> 00:12:55.550
We're in no danger for them.

00:12:55.650 --> 00:12:58.210
They're harmless, unless the chemicals from the two different drums come together.

00:12:58.710 --> 00:12:59.570
Let's get out of here.

00:12:59.650 --> 00:12:59.790
Lay.

00:13:00.220 --> 00:13:03.940
I'm nearly even here till I find out the meaning of the telegrams and who sent them.

00:13:04.400 --> 00:13:07.300
I sent them and you answered my call, you fools.

00:13:08.360 --> 00:13:13.240
I mean to destroy you all, which is a blow at your various industries that will echo through the country.

00:13:13.590 --> 00:13:15.190
A lesson to others of your type.

00:13:15.860 --> 00:13:19.340
Too bad, Westfall, your new invention will prove to be your executioner.

00:13:19.660 --> 00:13:21.300
I will bring the two chemicals together.

00:13:21.950 --> 00:13:26.380
Then shall we call it the embrace of death for all of you.

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:32.820
Get him! He's the guilty one!

00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:46.770
Roll one of those cylinders into position.

00:13:46.970 --> 00:13:48.610
We'd better not. The boss is in there.

00:13:48.790 --> 00:13:50.790
He'll take care of himself. Do as I tell you.

00:13:58.220 --> 00:13:59.970
There's something out there. I'll only...

00:14:00.030 --> 00:14:04.220
chances to deal with them. Let them know that anything they do to us will only kick back

00:14:04.220 --> 00:14:09.560
on the man they're working for. I tell you why, not the gargoyle. Don't do it. We'll

00:14:09.560 --> 00:14:15.500
be killed. I'll risk it. Open up. I want to deal with you. Open it up. We'll see what

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:25.780
he wants. Look here, men. I want you to know we have the man you're working for in there

00:14:25.780 --> 00:14:29.970
with us. If you kill us, you'll kill him. Watch your eyes.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:33.970
You want an answer, huh? Well, here it is.

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:51.100
That's about right.

00:14:52.230 --> 00:14:53.730
How'd I put them closer together?

00:14:54.400 --> 00:14:56.500
Listen, you sap, we gotta have time to get out of here.

00:14:57.720 --> 00:14:58.700
Get me those pliers some.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:31.120
You're the worst man that fights us!

00:15:42.620 --> 00:15:43.100
Go out that one!

00:15:44.530 --> 00:15:45.150
Time to kill us!

00:16:04.700 --> 00:16:05.660
We must risk it!

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:55.230
of death. Could this be another murder trap? How can the girl escape? The gargoyle is gloating

00:16:55.230 --> 00:16:59.970
over his prisoners, but the girl is not afraid. Learn the gargoyle.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:05.890
Boyle's identity in The Payoff, next week's concluding chapter of The Spider Return.
